    "turn_file": "/shared/3/projects/podcasts/transcriptionQueue/turns/pol_appearance_episodes_interviews/9/1/91224.jsonl",
    "turn_idx": 13,
    "turn_text": "Thanks. But that is what the McCain campaign, that's their current tactic, as opposed to strategy. You see, is attack, attack, attack. And there is audio floating around of John McCain saying, you know, in a political campaign, when the facts aren't on your side, you go negative. And that's all they're doing now. So Sarah Palin is the pit bull wearing lipstick, I suppose, these days out there saying that Barack Obama is paling around with terrorists. She's out there paling around with the terrorists because she's got nothing else to say. And what she was reading a copy of the New York Times, my God, co-figure. Well, all along, I've been saying, when is the Obama camp going to start touting John McCain's involvement in the Keating Five. After all, without John McCain, it would have been the Keating Four, right? Well, I guess the time is now. See, I'm always talking about how smart the Republicans are, and I'm not talking about their candidates. I'm not talking about the people that they actually run for president because those seem to just be the puppets. I'm talking about the neocons who are behind the curtain pulling strings, if you know what I mean. Well, the thing about Barack Obama, he is a brilliant man himself. And you got to know they've been strategizing. And I guess now we're in the home stretch, right? We're in the final four weeks before the election. And guess what? This morning, the Obama campaign launched a new website. And the URL is Keatingeconomics.com. And it comes complete with its own 13 and a half minute documentary. And yes, I will link to it from the blog. And I will post the actual video right there on the blog. Your goal is to send this to as many people as you can because everyone needs to understand how deep in the muck John McCain is when it comes to this financial crisis because he was right in the thick of the last one too. And I'm talking about the SNL scandal. In fact, I'll just read you a little bit from this website, Keating Economics, John McCain and the making of a financial crisis. The current economic crisis demands that we understand John McCain's attitudes about economic oversight and corporate influence in federal regulation. Nothing illustrates the danger of his approach more clearly than his central role in the savings and loans scandal of the late 80s and early 90s. John McCain was accused of improperly aiding his political patron, Charles Keating, chairman of the Lincoln Savings and Loan Association. The bipartisan Senate Ethics Committee launched investigations and formally reprimanded Senator McCain for his role in the scandal, the first such senator to receive a major party nomination for president. At the heart of the scandal was Keating's Lincoln Savings and Loan Association, which took advantage of deregulation in the 1980s to make risky investments with its depositors money. McCain intervened on behalf of Charles Keating with federal regulators tasked with preventing banking fraud and champion legislation to delay regulation of the savings and loan industry, actions that allowed Keating to continue his fraud at an incredible cost to taxpayers. When the savings and loan industry collapsed, Keating's failed company put taxpayers on the hook for $3.4 billion and more than 20,000 Americans lost their savings. John McCain was reprimanded by the Bipartisan Senate Ethics Committee, but the ultimate cost of the crisis to American taxpayers reached more than $120 billion. The Keating scandal is eerily similar to today's credit crisis. where a lack of regulation and cozy relationships between the financial industry and Congress has allowed banks to make risky loans and profit by bending the rules. And in both cases, John McCain's judgment and values have placed him on the wrong side of history. I love that not only did this website appear today but it says right there at the bottom paid for by Obama for America. The website is Keatingeconomics.com and again you can watch the video there or I have it right there embedded on my blog today at RadioOrNot.com. This is what I've been waiting for and I guess it's what the Obama campaign was waiting for too because this is their October surprise all along I've been saying The Keating Five. What about the Keating Five? And I guess they were just waiting for the right moment. And the moment is now four weeks out from the election and good for them. All right. I promised you on Friday that over the weekend I was going to be speaking with former Florida Governor, former Florida Senator Bob Graham. He and I played phone tag all weekend. But I finally, the reason I'm getting the show out so late is because we finally got to speak this afternoon. Senator Graham, do we call you Senator or Governor? How do I refer to you?",
