      }
    ],
    "turn_type_label": "Substantive",
    "conversation_move_label": "Assert / Elaborate"
  },
  {
    "episode_id": 91224,
    "turn_file": "/shared/3/projects/podcasts/transcriptionQueue/turns/pol_appearance_episodes_interviews/9/1/91224.jsonl",
    "turn_idx": 33,
    "turn_text": "Yeah, if we could turn back the clock, I'd say that often. Unfortunately, we can't. But the next best thing would be, I think, getting Barack Obama in there to start bringing us back to that place. The most hypocritical thing that keeps coming into my mind is Republicans claim that they are the party of fiscal responsibility and smaller government and less spending, yet look what's happened over the last eight years. It's been massive spending, and we're in debt. you know, from, for an administration that inherited a surplus to have us with this kind of a debt saddled on our kids and grandchildren is unconscionable and yet they still, they still spew that party line and pretend that, that they didn't put us in this position. How do you, how do they reconcile that?",
    "speaker_id": "SPEAKER_03",
    "inferred_speaker_name": null,
    "inferred_speaker_role": null,
    "chosen_text_key": "transcript",
    "explicit_propositions": [
      {
        "text": "The U.S. has experienced massive government spending over the last eight years.",
        "confidence": 0.96
      },
      {
        "text": "Time travel is impossible.",
        "confidence": 0.95
      },
      {
        "text": "Republicans claim to support fiscal responsibility, smaller government, and reduced spending.",
        "confidence": 0.94
      },
      {
        "text": "The current level of national debt will burden future generations.",
        "confidence": 0.93
      },
      {
        "text": "I often express regret about past decisions.",
        "confidence": 0.92
      },
      {
        "text": "It is morally unacceptable for the nation to pass large debts onto children and grandchildren.",
        "confidence": 0.91
      },
      {
        "text": "The previous administration inherited a budget surplus.",
        "confidence": 0.9
      },
      {
        "text": "Republican leaders continue to promote their stated principles despite contradictory actions.",
        "confidence": 0.89
      },
      {
        "text": "Republican leadership pretends they were not responsible for the current debt crisis.",
        "confidence": 0.88
      },
      {
        "text": "Barack Obama should be involved in efforts to restore national policy direction.",
        "confidence": 0.87
      }
    ],
    "assumptions": [
      {
        "text": "Fiscal responsibility requires consistent alignment between political rhetoric and actual spending behavior.",
        "confidence": 0.94
      },
      {
        "text": "Future generations deserve economic stability and fairness from present decision-makers.",
        "confidence": 0.92
      },
      {
        "text": "Public discourse should hold politicians accountable for contradictions between promises and outcomes.",
        "confidence": 0.91
      },
      {
        "text": "Restoring policies from the Obama era represents a viable path toward fiscal recovery.",
        "confidence": 0.9
      },
      {
        "text": "Political hypocrisy undermines public trust in institutions.",
        "confidence": 0.89
