    "turn_idx": 37,
    "turn_text": "Right. Well, that's what I mean. A lot of people are saying myself included is that my problem with this bailout bill that passed is it seems to be, again, relief for those at the top. What about those on the bottom? I mean, I'll speak for myself. I'm a single mother. I have a nine year old in Florida schools, which is something else I would love to talk to you about. And I just lost my job. I'm trying to make a go of it on my own. But in this economy, more and more people are being put in the position that I'm in, where now I'm going to struggle to keep us insured. But that my health benefits under Cobra are prohibitively expensive at a time when my income has been slashed. And I still have to worry about paying my mortgage each month. And the thing is it's not just me, more and more people. It's seemingly on a weekly basis are in the same position I'm in. And this bill doesn't give us any relief.",
