  {
    "episode_id": 91224,
    "turn_file": "/shared/3/projects/podcasts/transcriptionQueue/turns/pol_appearance_episodes_interviews/9/1/91224.jsonl",
    "turn_idx": 57,
    "turn_text": "Well, I bet. I have these little sort of fantasies. I think about writing a book, if I had the discipline to do it, on where we would be today if the Supreme Court hadn't stepped in and ruled in favor of George Bush in Bush v. Gore. And perhaps even if John Kerry had chosen Bob Graham as his running mate, I think we would have been in a different place today. And I guess sometimes you just can't even do that because just we were like we were talking about turning back the clock to the Clinton years. It's not going to happen. We have to look ahead and think, well, what we can do now to get out of the mess that we're in. I do want to ask you, you know, you spent many years as governor of Florida and the education system in the state is really quite sad. What the legislature has done in terms of cutting funding to our schools, I think, borders on criminal. They say that they'll hold education harmless yet with each meeting of the legislature. It seems they slash more funds from education to the point now where Florida is 50th out of 50 states in per capita funding per student. What do you think about where Florida education is right now?",
    "speaker_id": "SPEAKER_03",
    "inferred_speaker_name": null,
    "inferred_speaker_role": null,
    "chosen_text_key": "transcript",
